{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788353901762,"sessionID":"ses_f9dd039ddffeMv7fklzwEjK3To","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_592cc8bf798b445db50c893b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # CANNBench operator patterns\n2: \n3: These patterns describe the nine vendored operators. Task files remain the\n4: normative source.\n5: \n6: ## Common elementwise path\n7: \n8: `sigmoid`, `exp`, `mish`, and `gelu` flatten arbitrary-rank contiguous input to\n9: one dimension. Use grid-stride tiles, `real_shape=[n]` tails, f32 intermediates\n10: for f16/bf16 where needed, and `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`. Stable forms must\n11: preserve NaN and Inf behavior from `golden.py`. GELU has both `none` and `tanh`\n12: attributes and may require distinct kernels or tile widths.\n13: \n14: Pinned-v2 scalar rule: both data branches of `asc2.where(condition, a, b)`\n15: must be LocalTensor values. A Python scalar branch such as\n16: `asc2.where(x >= 0, 1.0, tile)` fails with `AttributeError: 'float' object has\n17: no attribute 'dtype'`. Prefer algebra that avoids the select, or build an\n18: aligned tensor branch with `asc2.full`.\n19: \n20: ## MaskedScale\n21: \n22: Cover every cross-product present in `cases.yaml`: x is f16/bf16/f32; mask is\n23: int8/uint8/f16/bf16/f32. Direct vector arithmetic on int8 is unsupported in the\n24: observed runtime; cast int8 to f16 and then f32. Torch uint8 can be reinterpreted\n25: as int8 without copying, but values 128..255 then require an in-kernel f32 +256\n26: correction. Avoid f16 and bf16 temporaries coexisting in one specialization;\n27: use a two-kernel f32 bridge for cross-half combinations.\n28: \n29: ## SwiGLU\n30: \n31: Split the selected even-sized dimension and compute `silu(x0) * x1`. Map the\n32: contiguous N-D tensor to `[outer, 2 * half_cols]` without materializing aligned\n33: halves. Two-dimensional copy operations require a 32-byte-aligned final tile\n34: dimension. Degenerate `half_cols` therefore needs a separately evidenced path.\n35: The current official result is 18/20: case 9 is an NPU runtime failure around\n36: the host narrow/contiguous fallback and case 12 is a bf16 NaN-position\n37: mismatch. Treat both roots as suspected until reproduced on hardware; a prior\n38: replacement fallback regressed to 0/20 and must not be copied.\n39: \n40: ## ForeachAddcdivScalar\n41: \n42: Loop over tensor lists on the host and launch one elementwise kernel for each\n43: triple. Preserve scalar zero, Inf, and NaN behavior. Compute division in f32\n44: for half inputs and cast once on output.\n45: \n46: ## ForeachNorm\n47: \n48: Return one 0-D result per input tensor. Specialize host dispatch by p, including\n49: negative p and Inf. Cross-core sum/max needs `asc2.atomic_add` or\n50: `asc2.atomic_max`; pad scalar storage to at least 32 bytes. A loop-carried\n51: accumulator must be seeded with a pyasc scalar/tile result, not a Python float.\n52: Use only `asc2.range` kwargs confirmed by the pinned source.\n53: \n54: ## RMSNorm\n55: \n56: Normalize each last-dimension row and multiply by gamma. The pinned v2 source\n57: contains `asc2.rms_norm`; the current canonical module uses it for the main\n58: path, with an f16 hop for bf16, and a manual fallback for shapes that fail its\n59: constraints. Preserve f32 accumulation where the manual path is used. Cover D\n60: from 2 through 8192, including prime/non-aligned tails and special values.\n61: \n62: Reduction scalars are PlainValue results. `asc2.rsqrt(plain_value)` rejects the\n63: input because `rsqrt` requires LocalTensor. Use scalar arithmetic supported by\n64: the pinned API (for example `1.0 / asc2.sqrt(plain_value)`) or broadcast the\n65: value into an aligned local tensor before a tensor-only unary op. Budget that\n66: broadcast as a live f32 tile: a generated `tile_d=2048` manual RMSNorm used\n67: 279–329 KB and overflowed the 253952 B UB.\n\n(End of file - total 67 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# CANNBench operator patterns\n\nThese patterns describe the nine vendored operators. Task files remain the\nnormative source.\n\n## Common elementwise path\n\n`sigmoid`, `exp`, `mish`, and `gelu` flatten arbitrary-rank contiguous input to\none dimension. Use grid-stride tiles, `real_shape=[n]` tails, f32 intermediates\nfor f16/bf16 where needed, and `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`. Stable forms must\npreserve NaN and Inf behavior from `golden.py`. GELU has both `none` and `tanh`\nattributes and may require distinct kernels or tile widths.\n\nPinned-v2 scalar rule: both data branches of `asc2.where(condition, a, b)`\nmust be LocalTensor values. A Python scalar branch such as\n`asc2.where(x >= 0, 1.0, tile)` fails with `AttributeError: 'float' object has\nno attribute 'dtype'`. Prefer algebra that avoids the select, or build an\naligned tensor branch with `asc2.full`.\n\n## MaskedScale","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md","text":"# CANNBench operator patterns\n\nThese patterns describe the nine vendored operators. Task files remain the\nnormative source.\n\n## Common elementwise path\n\n`sigmoid`, `exp`, `mish`, and `gelu` flatten arbitrary-rank contiguous input to\none dimension. Use grid-stride tiles, `real_shape=[n]` tails, f32 intermediates\nfor f16/bf16 where needed, and `cores = min(72, num_tiles)`. Stable forms must\npreserve NaN and Inf behavior from `golden.py`. GELU has both `none` and `tanh`\nattributes and may require distinct kernels or tile widths.\n\nPinned-v2 scalar rule: both data branches of `asc2.where(condition, a, b)`\nmust be LocalTensor values. A Python scalar branch such as\n`asc2.where(x >= 0, 1.0, tile)` fails with `AttributeError: 'float' object has\nno attribute 'dtype'`. Prefer algebra that avoids the select, or build an\naligned tensor branch with `asc2.full`.\n\n## MaskedScale\n\nCover every cross-product present in `cases.yaml`: x is f16/bf16/f32; mask is\nint8/uint8/f16/bf16/f32. Direct vector arithmetic on int8 is unsupported in the\nobserved runtime; cast int8 to f16 and then f32. Torch uint8 can be reinterpreted\nas int8 without copying, but values 128..255 then require an in-kernel f32 +256\ncorrection. Avoid f16 and bf16 temporaries coexisting in one specialization;\nuse a two-kernel f32 bridge for cross-half combinations.\n\n## SwiGLU\n\nSplit the selected even-sized dimension and compute `silu(x0) * x1`. Map the\ncontiguous N-D tensor to `[outer, 2 * half_cols]` without materializing aligned\nhalves. Two-dimensional copy operations require a 32-byte-aligned final tile\ndimension. Degenerate `half_cols` therefore needs a separately evidenced path.\nThe current official result is 18/20: case 9 is an NPU runtime failure around\nthe host narrow/contiguous fallback and case 12 is a bf16 NaN-position\nmismatch. Treat both roots as suspected until reproduced on hardware; a prior\nreplacement fallback regressed to 0/20 and must not be copied.\n\n## ForeachAddcdivScalar\n\nLoop over tensor lists on the host and launch one elementwise kernel for each\ntriple. Preserve scalar zero, Inf, and NaN behavior. Compute division in f32\nfor half inputs and cast once on output.\n\n## ForeachNorm\n\nReturn one 0-D result per input tensor. Specialize host dispatch by p, including\nnegative p and Inf. Cross-core sum/max needs `asc2.atomic_add` or\n`asc2.atomic_max`; pad scalar storage to at least 32 bytes. A loop-carried\naccumulator must be seeded with a pyasc scalar/tile result, not a Python float.\nUse only `asc2.range` kwargs confirmed by the pinned source.\n\n## RMSNorm\n\nNormalize each last-dimension row and multiply by gamma. The pinned v2 source\ncontains `asc2.rms_norm`; the current canonical module uses it for the main\npath, with an f16 hop for bf16, and a manual fallback for shapes that fail its\nconstraints. Preserve f32 accumulation where the manual path is used. Cover D\nfrom 2 through 8192, including prime/non-aligned tails and special values.\n\nReduction scalars are PlainValue results. `asc2.rsqrt(plain_value)` rejects the\ninput because `rsqrt` requires LocalTensor. Use scalar arithmetic supported by\nthe pinned API (for example `1.0 / asc2.sqrt(plain_value)`) or broadcast the\nvalue into an aligned local tensor before a tensor-only unary op. Budget that\nbroadcast as a live f32 tile: a generated `tile_d=2048` manual RMSNorm used\n279–329 KB and overflowed the 253952 B UB.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":67,"totalLines":67,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md","time":{"start":1788353901756,"end":1788353901761}},"id":"prt_06232f38d0012Vo6BImA0ljG9i","sessionID":"ses_f9dd039ddffeMv7fklzwEjK3To","messageID":"msg_0622fe0ab001SfCeriaSYvrkxH"}}
