{"type":"text","timestamp":1788353948365,"sessionID":"ses_f9dd039ddffeMv7fklzwEjK3To","part":{"id":"prt_062338fe4001QLAZAJm6eersPt","messageID":"msg_06232f4df001oMnkkWwL3Kbmnd","sessionID":"ses_f9dd039ddffeMv7fklzwEjK3To","type":"text","text":"I've now reviewed all the key materials. Let me analyze the candidate against the contract:\n\n**Review findings:**\n\n1. **Public contract** — `rms_norm(x, gamma, epsilon=1e-6) -> Tensor y`: signature, defaults, and return match exactly. ✅\n2. **Host/JIT boundary** — Host uses only `ensure_npu_platform()`, `.is_contiguous()`, `.contiguous()`, `.shape`, `.numel()`, `torch.empty_like`, Python float arithmetic for `inv_D`. No torch math. ✅\n3. **Tails** — `n = tile_d if od + tile_d <= D else D - od` with `real_shape=[n]` in both `copy_in` and `copy_out`. Covers prime/non-aligned D (cases 6,7,8,9,10,11,12,13,16). ✅\n4. **Dtypes** — f16/bf16 promoted to f32 via `x.to(asc.float32)` / `g.to(asc.float32)`, computed in f32, cast back via `y.to(x.dtype)`. Matches golden's f32 accumulation. ✅\n5. **Special values** — No clamping; IEEE inf/nan/zero propagate naturally through `xf * xf`, `rsqrt`, multiply. All-zero rows (case 17) produce `rsqrt(epsilon)` × 0 = 0. ✅\n6. **UB budget** — `tile_d=1024`. The operator-patterns reference warns that `tile_d=2048` overflowed UB (279–329 KB > 253952 B). At 1024, usage scales to ~140–165 KB, safely under 253952 B. ✅\n7. **`asc2.rsqrt(plain_value)` rejection** — The reference explicitly states `rsqrt` requires LocalTensor, not PlainValue. The candidate correctly broadcasts the scalar via `asc2.full([tile_d], scalar, dtype=asc.float32)` before calling `asc2.rsqrt` — this is one of the two recommended approaches. ✅\n8. **Loop-carried accumulator** — Seeded with `asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full([1, 64], 0.0, dtype=asc.float32))` exactly as the verified pattern requires. ✅\n9. **Grid-stride** — `for r in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), S, asc2.block_num())` distributes rows; `cores = min(72, S)`. ✅\n10. **No forbidden patterns** — No `break`/`continue`/`return`/`print`/imports/`math.*`/`range()` inside `@asc2.jit`. ✅\n\nNo fixes needed. Running the syntax check:","time":{"start":1788353941476,"end":1788353948364}}}
